;; Mechanically transcribed static XKB symbol evidence for the frozen Manna
;; Cadet baseline.  See docs/manna-cadet-baseline.md and
;; tools/manna-truth-table.lisp for the frozen hashes and raw keysyms.
;;
;; The eight table cells use the documented case/script/plane order.  The
;; static Top XKB group is TWO_LEVEL: its Greek+Top cells therefore repeat its
;; observed Top symbol.  This records symbol selection only.  The primary
;; layered function table below is also transcribed. Its realization allocates
;; the frozen carriers.  The direct one-key Greek and Top selectors below have
;; an exact immediate held lifecycle; tap-hold activation and all other timing
;; remain explicitly unresolved.
;; Static XKB tables.  NAMED-SYMBOL is a semantic registry name, not an XKB
;; keysym escape hatch; the raw source spelling remains in the frozen truth
;; table.  Unicode scalars and named keys are recorded directly.
;; Both frozen primary normal layers retain lshift and rshift as direct
;; physical keys.  Each contributes the same held case state; owner-scoped
;; lifetime means releasing either source cannot clear the other source's
;; contribution.  The home-row Shift aliases are separate tap-holds and are
;; deliberately not represented here.
;; Both frozen primary layered variants map their direct lctl source position
;; to the Greek carrier and direct rctl to the Top carrier.  Unlike the
;; Delete/Enter aliases, these source paths have no tap-hold timing or
;; arbitration: they immediately select their state while physically held.
;; The interaction consumes the selector position and restores the documented
;; initial axis state on release.  Backend spellings and carrier numbers live
;; exclusively in the device/profile realization.
;; The frozen primary layered files contain this entire function table.  It
;; is a semantic patch, not a Kanata layer spelling.  The two 200 ms
;; tap-hold activators (End and PgDn) and their cancellation policy are not
;; represented here: no activation behavior is guessed from Kanata.
;; These function results have frozen alias identities and exact carrier
;; pairs.  They are named symbols rather than direct Unicode here so the
;; realization—not the layout—owns the carrier/XKB spelling.
;; The shared logical mode-key denotes the same physical location in both
;; devices.  Its inactive result differs (Menu on Advantage 2, Caps Lock
;; on Advantage 360), so only its common active function result is stated.
;; These primary normal-layer inputs have direct, context-independent tap
;; identities.  Their held interpretation is carried only by the explicit
;; unselected interactions below; no backend token or timing policy lives
;; in these ordinary bindings.
;; Both frozen primary normal layers select exactly these sixteen
;; TAP-HOLD-RELEASE aliases.  The source establishes their literal taps,
;; semantic held resources, and equal timeout pairs (250 ms only for A);
;; it does not select an interaction-compatibility policy, Kanata action,
;; allocation, backend grade, or artifact-emission path.  Delete and Enter
;; are transcribed because both normal layers select gdel/rtop, but the
;; buffered policy still explicitly refuses them for lack of direct traces.
;; The physical defsrc token is ent; RETURN is its existing shared logical
;; position.  Do not add an ENTER topology position merely for this alias.
;; The frozen navigation rows and the four Advantage 360 local hotkeys are
;; context-independent named-key routes.  The hotkey bindings are part of the
;; shared logical layout even though the Advantage 2 placement explicitly
;; classifies those four positions as unreachable; compilation must retain
;; that reviewed device difference rather than inventing inputs for it.

(ivory-key 1)
(define-layout
  manna-cadet
  (uses-topology kinesis-advantage)
  (axis case (:states plain shifted) (:resolution product))
  (axis script (:states roman greek) (:resolution product))
  (axis plane (:states base top) (:resolution product))
  (axis function (:states inactive active) (:resolution patch))
  (level-order case script plane)
  (modifiers control meta super hyper alt)
  (binding
    number-1
    (at (plain roman base) (unicode "1"))
    (at (shifted roman base) (named-symbol exclam))
    (at (plain greek base) (named-symbol dagger))
    (at (shifted greek base) none)
    (at (plain roman top) none)
    (at (shifted roman top) none)
    (at (plain greek top) none)
    (at (shifted greek top) none)
  )
